{
  "name": "regex-ascii-classes",
  "description": "Regex character classes are ASCII only, as in Dart's RegExp (ECMAScript, no `u` flag): `\\d`/`\\D` see only 0-9 and `\\w`/`\\W` only A-Z, a-z, 0-9 and `_`. Arabic-Indic digits (U+0663-U+0665) are not `\\d` and the accented e (U+00E9) is not `\\w`, also inside a character class (`[\\w]`) and in the `matches` BoolExpr op. Each replace-mode regex wraps every match (`{{value}}`) in brackets. Every input reads page state, so the engine keeps the Values unresolved with `watches` and the client resolves them.",
  "input": {
    "type": "Column",
    "key": "col",
    "children": [
      {
        "type": "Text",
        "key": "d",
        "props": {
          "data": {
            "type": "transform",
            "input": {
              "type": "state",
              "scope": "page",
              "key": "digits"
            },
            "by": [
              {
                "type": "regex",
                "pattern": "\\d+",
                "flags": "g",
                "replacement": "[{{value}}]"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
